+# Bots, projects and Jarvis: text for the Help sheet and README (merge by hand)
+
+Deep links: `#projects-live`, `#market-hours`. Code: `planner/ext-projects.js` (an add-on file, loaded by one `<script defer>` tag). Tests: `planner/tests/projects.test.js`. No new synced collection: everything new is kept on this device under its own keys, and your planner data is only read.
+
+## Help sheet bullets (one line each, same style as the others)
+- **Bots and projects** (a line on Today, `#projects-live`, All tools, or "bots and projects" in Find): the live status of your NQ bots (Zlarior on the MFFU 50K, ATLAS and BLITZ on their 25Ks: today's P&L, room above the floor, what is left to the target, the session) and of the Kalshi bot (balance, today, open positions), read from what your PC publishes. It also shows the NQ market clock, which projects are late or blocked, and one-tap links to **Zenith**, **Kalshi** and **Jarvis**. On Today it is one line, for example "Bot stopped · Kalshi $512 · 2 projects flagged"; tap it for the card. The line moves up to **Needs you now** (still one line) only when a bot is stopped or has gone quiet during its own trading hours (2am to 3:30pm New York time on weekdays); you can switch that off.
+- **Market hours** (`#market-hours`, All tools): when NQ trades (Sunday 6pm to Friday 5pm New York time, with a 5-6pm break on weekdays) and when the bots can enter, with the time left until the next change, in New York time and in your phone's time. Switch on **Show NQ hours on the Day and Week views** to see the bots' window as a thin purple line and the closed hours as light stripes behind your events. It is off until you turn it on.
+- **Projects** now starts with **At a glance**: one chip per project, green, amber or red, saying why ("blocked", "milestone 2 days late", "2 overdue", "stopped"). Tap a chip to jump to the project. Projects with a dashboard (NQ bot, Kalshi, Jarvis) get a live line and a link.
+- **Inside Jarvis** the Planner starts dark, to match Jarvis, until you choose an appearance yourself (Settings, or the sun and moon button). Your own choice always wins, and nothing is saved by this.
+- **Jarvis** (in the More menu on a phone, and on the Bots and projects card): opens your hub. Jarvis reads today's events and tasks from this phone, so its Planner card stays right even when the Planner changes how it stores things.
+
+## README additions
+### Bots and projects (`#projects-live`)
+- Sources, both optional and both read-only: the NQ bots' `live.json` (branch `live` of nq-dashboard: `board.lit`, `board.atlas`, `board.blitz` or the top-level `blitz`, and `pc_verdict`) and the Kalshi bot's `kalshi.json` (its own repo, `demetrades2000-coder/kalshi-feed`, branch `main`: `balance`, `today_pnl`, `positions`, `running`, `mode`, `t`). Each is read from raw.githubusercontent.com first and the GitHub API second; a 404 means "not connected yet".
+- It checks when the app opens or comes back to the screen, then every 3 minutes while Today, Projects or the sheet is showing (every 12 minutes otherwise). Refresh checks now. Requests time out after 8 seconds and never show an error on their own: offline, the card shows the last good copy and says "Offline: showing the last copies".
+- States: a bot's line is green when the PC says it is running, red when it is stopped, amber when it needs a look, and "not updating" when the PC has not published for 20 minutes (grey outside the bots' hours). Kalshi is "running" when its file is under 15 minutes old.
+- Needs you now: only inside the bots' window on a weekday, only right after a successful read, and only if "Put a stopped or silent bot under Needs you now" is on (it is by default). An old copy read while offline never raises it. It stays one folded line there too (the busy day of `todayorg.test.js` with live data present grows by about 45 px, not by the whole card).
+- Project health: blocked or a milestone past due is red; overdue tasks, a milestone due within 3 days, a stopped or silent bot, or Kalshi not updating are amber or red; paused is grey. Projects are matched to their dashboards by name (NQ, Zlarior, ATLAS, BLITZ and Zenith go to Zenith; Kalshi; Jarvis).
+- **Not in your Planner yet**: the sheet offers Zenith and Ascend (coming soon) when no project matches them. The button opens the Planner's own project sheet filled in; nothing is saved until you press Save.
+- Links are `../` (Zenith), `../kalshi/` and `../jarvis/` on the dashboard site (the public site addresses anywhere else) and open in the same tab. Inside Jarvis (the Planner in a Jarvis frame on the same site, with `window.__jarvis`), Zenith, Kalshi and **Back to Jarvis** call `__jarvis.show('zenith' | 'kalshi' | 'home')`, so Jarvis switches apps itself and is never replaced.
+
+### Market hours (`#market-hours`)
+- Worked out in New York time with the planner's own ET converter, so daylight-saving changes and a phone in another time zone are handled. CME holidays are not checked here; early closes from the dashboard data already show on the calendar.
+- The Day and Week bands are drawn when the view is drawn and never stored. They sit behind your events, so nothing moves or gets covered.
+
+### Jarvis summary (`localStorage['planner.today.v1']`)
+- `{ v: 1, day: 'YYYY-MM-DD', events: [{ title, start: 'HH:MM' or '', end: 'HH:MM' or '', allDay }], tasks: [{ title, due: 'YYYY-MM-DD', done }], updated: ms }`.
+- Events are what the calendar shows on that day (repeats included; hidden event types and market layers left out; bot and market feed items skipped), all-day first, up to 40. Tasks are the ones due that day (done or not) and the open overdue ones, open first, up to 60. Times are the phone's local wall-clock times, like the rest of the planner.
+- Rewritten whenever the planner saves or draws and the day's list changed, at midnight, and when the app is shown, hidden or closed. Jarvis on the same site reads it (its `storage` listener already reacts to `planner.*` keys).
+
+### Phone header and Jarvis
+- At 640 px and narrower, the header icons share one row and never cover the logo (they shrink from 36 px to about 30 px when space is tight); offline, the Offline pill takes the logo's place. CSS only, in the small `<style>` next to the add-on's script tag.
+- Inside Jarvis (a same-site frame whose page has `window.__jarvis`) with no appearance chosen (`planner.theme` unset), a small script in `<head>` marks `<html data-jarvis>` and applies the dark theme before the first paint, and `thPref()` treats unset + `data-jarvis` as dark for that session. `planner.theme` is never written, so Settings or the sun and moon button still decide.
+
+## For developers
+- `index.html` changes: the add-on's `<script defer>` tag, the Jarvis dark script and the phone header `<style>` in `<head>`, one line in `thPref()`, and the hooks below.
+- Add-on hook (the EXT block in `index.html`): an add-on file queues `(window.PLANNER_EXT = window.PLANNER_EXT || []).push((api) => { ... })`. `api` reads the planner (`state()`, `eventsOn()`, date and ET helpers), adds a Today card (`card(def, beforeId)`, same shape as `TO_CARDS`), an All tools tile (`tool`), a palette command (`cmd`), re-applies the theme (`theme()`), and listens to `on('save' | 'render' | 'route', fn)`: `save()` emits save, `afterMain()` emits render, `route()` offers each deep link first (a handler returns true when the link is its own). Add-ons never write planner data themselves.
+- Device-only keys: `planner.ext.projects` (settings: `nq`, `kalshi`, `flag`, `bands`), `planner.ext.live` and `planner.ext.kalshi` (last good copies, slimmed), `planner.today.v1` (the Jarvis summary). Not synced, not in Back up.
+- Test hook: with `window.PLANNER_TEST`, `window.__xp` exposes `market`, `marketLine`, `slim`, `kslim`, `health`, `todaySummary`, `botAlert`, `bandsFor` and the feed state.
+- `projects.test.js` (PORT default 8792) mocks both feeds and covers: escalation inside and outside the bots' hours, the flag switch, offline copies, the market clock (Saturday, Sunday evening, Monday 1am, the Tuesday break, Friday 5pm, a Los Angeles phone), the bands, the Jarvis summary (shape, repeats, hidden types, a task added in the app, the midnight rollover), deep links, Find, All tools, Customize Today, adding Zenith through the Planner's own sheet, dark mode, and that the add-on only adds its own keys and leaves `planner.v1` exactly as it is.
